<title>USA: S&amp;P cuts Hawaii GO bonds to A-plus from AA.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P cuts Hawaii GO bonds to A-plus from AA.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp said Friday it cut Hawaii's general obligation bond rating to A-plus from AA, affecting $2.5 billion of debt.</p>
<p>The rating was taken off CreditWatch, where it was placed on December 11, 1996.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said it has assigned its A-plus rating to the state $350 million GO bonds of 1997 Series CN due 2017 and $250 million GO refunding bonds of 1997 series CO due 2011.</p>
<p>The downgrade reflects the state's rising debt levels, with substantial additional debt likely for the next bienniumn, and deteriorating financial performance.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
